# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EOL policy: LF in the index, LF on disk, on every platform.
#
# Why this file exists (the PIN-hash integrity story):
# src/renderer/i18n/ui-locale-bundles/ holds bundles vendored byte-for-byte
# from phlix-ui, SHA-256-pinned in the PIN manifest. tests/unit/
# i18nLocales.test.ts hashes the WORKING-TREE bytes of each vendored file
# against that pin. Git-for-Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so on a
# windows-latest CI checkout the LF blobs were silently rewritten to CRLF on
# disk before hashing — the pin test failed on Windows while ubuntu passed.
# The committed blobs were always LF; the checkout conversion was the bug.
#
# .gitattributes settings take precedence over core.autocrlf, so pinning the
# policy here makes the vendored bytes (and every other text file) identical
# on disk in every clone, dev machine, and CI shard — and keeps the PIN test
# strict (byte-exact) instead of forcing it to tolerate CRLF.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Treat files as text by content: normalize to LF on commit, check out as LF.
# Covers src/** (vendored bundles, catalogs, tests), docs/**, *.md, JSON,
# lockfiles, YAML, scripts — the whole estate-standard text surface.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never EOL-normalized on add or checkout (a converted icon is
# a corrupted icon; `binary` also keeps them out of `git add --renormalize`).
*.png binary
*.ico binary
